{"school":{"dbn":"09X313","name":"I.S. 313 School of Leadership Development","boro":"Bronx","district":"09","district_label":"District 9","report_type":"EMS","report_types":"EMS","school_type":"Middle","grades":"6 to 8","status":"open","enrollment":104,"enrollment_year":"2024-25","address":"1600 WEBSTER AVENUE, BRONX, NY 10457","phone":"718-293-9048","website":"www.IS313.ORG","directory_url":"https://www.myschools.nyc/en/schools/middle-school/65518","accessibility":"Partially Accessible","overview":"Hey there! We are glad that you have taken an interest in becoming a 313 Lion and joining the Pride. At C.I.S 313, we seek to make everyday a rigorous and joyous experience for our students. Our core classes (Math, ELA, Science, & Social Studies) utilizes curricula that are culturally-relevant, engaging, and rigorous preparing our students to be critical thinkers in the classroom and beyond. C.I.S 313 proudly offers a variety of extra-curricular activities for all our students that include; Co-Ed Soccer, Co-Ed Volleyball, Debate Team, Co-Ed Flag Football, and Theater. C.I.S 313 bolsters a strong roster of partners that provide valuable experiences for the development of students ranging from rites of passage to learning to express ones self through music writing. C.I.S 313 is a small school that is responsive to its students and families, so if there is a club or experience that students or families want to see we work them to build it and make sure it is comes to life in our community. Students at C.I.S 313 attend field trips that highlight the vast beauty and learning that lives with in New York City and the surrounding area.","start_time":"08:19am","end_time":"02:39pm","languages":null,"subway":"B, D to 174-175th Sts","bus":"Bx1, Bx11, Bx15, Bx17, Bx18A, Bx18B, Bx2, Bx32, Bx41, Bx41-SBS, BxM4","shared_building":"1","neighborhood":"South Bronx","latitude":40.840495,"longitude":-73.904275,"coordinate_source":"geocoded","first_year":"2015-16","last_year":"2024-25"},"seri